WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.440
Movie

00:01.440 --> 00:06.240
Imaginary and complex numbers. Have you ever wondered what lies beyond the realm of the numbers?

00:06.240 --> 00:12.720
We know what if we told you there is a whole other world of numbers that exist outside of our usual numerical system

00:13.520 --> 00:20.380
As we journey through the landscape of mathematics. We often find ourselves venturing beyond the familiar terrain of real numbers

00:21.000 --> 00:25.280
We stumble upon the intriguing territories of imaginary and complex numbers

00:26.120 --> 00:27.680
Intriguing isn't it?

00:27.680 --> 00:32.220
Today we take a plunge into the fascinating world of imaginary and complex numbers

00:32.600 --> 00:35.640
Imagine a number when squared gives a negative result

00:36.440 --> 00:38.440
Impossible with real numbers, right?

00:38.560 --> 00:45.640
Welcome to the world of imaginary numbers. These numbers are not figments of our imagination, but a mathematical reality

00:45.880 --> 00:49.800
They're defined by the square root of negative 1 denoted as I

00:50.480 --> 00:56.000
Now if you're scratching your head, don't worry. It's a concept that challenges our understanding of numbers

00:56.320 --> 00:58.820
You see in the universe of numbers

00:59.360 --> 01:03.800
Imaginary numbers are like the elusive dark matter. They have strange properties

01:04.240 --> 01:10.660
For instance, they are the square roots of negative numbers. Yes, you heard it right where real numbers fail

01:11.200 --> 01:17.440
Imaginary numbers prevail so in the realm of imaginary numbers the impossible becomes possible

01:17.560 --> 01:23.840
What happens when you combine these imaginary numbers with our familiar real numbers you get complex numbers?

01:24.280 --> 01:26.920
Think of complex numbers as a dynamic duo

01:27.360 --> 01:30.160
comprised of a real part and an imaginary part

01:30.760 --> 01:32.760
represented in the form a plus by a

01:33.520 --> 01:41.200
Is our real number grounded in the tangible world while B is our imaginary number a concept that stretches beyond our usual

01:41.320 --> 01:42.800
understanding of numbers

01:42.800 --> 01:48.880
These two parts the real and the imaginary work together in harmony to create a complex number

01:49.320 --> 01:56.720
Each part holds its own unique properties yet when combined they form a number that can be manipulated and used in ways that real numbers

01:56.720 --> 01:58.720
alone cannot accomplish

01:58.800 --> 02:03.240
Complex numbers a blend of the real and the imaginary expand our numerical universe

02:03.680 --> 02:08.520
So we've journeyed beyond the familiar into the realm of the imaginary and the complex

02:09.100 --> 02:15.640
We've grappled with the intriguing concept of imaginary numbers a notion that transcends the constraints of reality

02:16.040 --> 02:21.360
We've explored their unique properties like how they behave when squared or multiplied

02:21.800 --> 02:27.000
we've delved into the realm of complex numbers comprised of real and imaginary parts and

02:27.360 --> 02:30.680
Discovered their fascinating characteristics in the end

02:31.400 --> 02:38.200
Imaginary and complex numbers are not merely mathematical curiosities. They're essential tools in understanding the world around us

